{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://www.bioassayontology.org/bao#BAO_0003053","ontology_name":"bao","ontology_prefix":"BAO","short_form":"BAO_0003053","description":[],"label":"PIPES","obo_id":"BAO:0003053","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_39033","ontology_name":"chebi","ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_39033","description":[],"label":"PIPES","obo_id":"CHEBI:39033","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_39033","ontology_name":"micro","ontology_prefix":"MICRO","short_form":"CHEBI_39033","description":[],"label":"PIPES","obo_id":"CHEBI:39033","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_39033","ontology_name":"slm","ontology_prefix":"SLM","short_form":"CHEBI_39033","description":[],"label":"PIPES","obo_id":"","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000077489","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["1,4 Diazacyclohexane","1,4 Piperazine","1,4-Diazacyclohexane","1,4-Piperazine","Piperazine Diacetate","Piperazine Dihydrochloride","Piperazine Hexahydrate","Piperazine Hydrate","Piperazine Hydrobromide","Piperazine Hydrochloride","Piperazine Monohydrochloride","Piperazine Phosphate (1:1)","Piperazine Phosphate Anhydrous","Piperazine Phosphate","Piperazine Salt","Piperazine Sulfate","Piperazine Tartrate (1:1), (R-(R*,R*))-isomer","Piperazine Tartrate","Piperazine Tartrate, (R-(R*,R*))-isomer","Piperazinium Oleate","Pripsen"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D000077489","description":["An anti-nematodal agent effective against the intestinal nematodes ASCARIS LUMBRICOIDES (roundworm) and ENTEROBIUS VERMICULARIS (pinworm, threadworm).  It produces a neuromuscular block leading to flaccid muscle paralysis in susceptible worms, which are then dislodged from the gut and expelled in feces."],"label":"Piperazine","obo_id":"mesh:D000077489","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D010878","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["AB Piperacillin","AB-Piperacillin","Cl 227193","Cl-227193","Cl227193","Curasan, Piperacillin","Monosodium Salt, Piperacillin","Pipcil","Pipera Hameln","Pipera-Hameln","Piperacillin Curasan","Piperacillin Fresenius","Piperacillin Hexal","Piperacillin Monosodium Salt","Piperacillin Ratiopharm","Piperacillin Sodium","Piperacillin-Ratiopharm","Pipercillin","Pipracil","Pipril","Salt, Piperacillin Monosodium","Sodium, Piperacillin","T 1220","T-1220","T1220"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D010878","description":["Semisynthetic, broad-spectrum, AMPICILLIN derived ureidopenicillin antibiotic proposed for PSEUDOMONAS infections. It is also used in combination with other antibiotics."],"label":"Piperacillin","obo_id":"mesh:D010878","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63106","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["N-(18-amino-18-oxo-3,6,9,12,15-pentaoxaoctadec-1-yl)-N(2)-{3-[2-(2-{[(1-{[1-({1-[(1-{3-[2-(2-{[4-(1H-indol-3-yl)butanoyl]amino}ethoxy)ethoxy]propanoyl}piperidin-4-yl)carbonyl]piperidin-4-yl}carbonyl)piperidin-4-yl]carbonyl}piperidin-4-yl)carbonyl]amino}ethoxy)ethoxy]propanoyl}-N(6)-(5-nitro-2-furoyl)lysinamide"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_63106","description":["A tetrapeptide that consists of four piperidine-4-carboxylic acid units (connected via amide linkages) where the amino terminus is acylated by a 3-[2-(2-{[4-(indol-3-yl)butanoyl]amino}ethoxy)ethoxy]propanoyl group and the carboxy terminus is formally condensed with the amino group of 3-[2-(2-aminoethoxy)ethoxy]propanoic acid, the carboxy group of which is in turn formally condensed with the α-amino group of \u003cem\u003eN\u003c/em\u003e\u003csmall\u003e\u003csup\u003e6\u003c/small\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e-5-nitrofuroyllysine bearing a polyether moiety at its carboxy terminus."],"label":"N-(18-amino-18-oxo-3,6,9,12,15-pentaoxaoctadec-1-yl)-N(2)-{3-[2-(2-{[(1-{[1-({1-[(1-{3-[2-(2-{[4-(indol-3-yl)butanoyl]amino}ethoxy)ethoxy]propanoyl}piperidin-4-yl)carbonyl]piperidin-4-yl}carbonyl)piperidi