p://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75250","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["-ethyl-5-oxo-2-(piperazin-1-yl)-5,8-dihydropyrido[2,3-d]pyrimidine-6-carboxylic acid","5,8-Dihydro-8-ethyl-5-oxo-2-(1-piperazinyl)pyrido(2,3-d)pyrimidine-6-carboxylic acid","8-Ethyl-5,8-dihydro-5-oxo-2-(1-piperazinyl)pyrido(2,3-d)pyrimidine-6-carboxylic acid","Deblaston","Dolcol","Filtrax","Memento 400","NSC-758160","Nuril","Pi-coli","Pipedac","Pipemid","Pipemidate","Pipemidic acid anhydrous","Pipemidic acid hydrate","Pipram","Pipurin","Tractur","Urosten","Uroval","acide pipemidique","acido pipemidico","acidum pipemidicum","pipemidic acid"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_75250","description":["A pyridopyrimidine that is 5-oxo-5,8-dihydropyrido[2,3-\u003cem\u003ed\u003c/em\u003e]pyrimidine-6-carboxylic acid substituted at position 2 by a piperazin-1-yl group and at position 8 by an ethyl group. A synthetic broad-spectrum antibacterial, it is used for treatment of gastrointestinal, biliary, and urinary infections."],"label":"pipemidic acid","obo_id":"CHEBI:75250","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["-ethyl-5-oxo-2-(piperazin-1-yl)-5,8-dihydropyrido[2,3-d]pyrimidine-6-carboxylic acid"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D017300","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Arduan","Bromide, Pipecurium","Bromide, Pipecuronium","Dibromide Pipecuronium","Dibromide, Dihydrate Pipecuronium","Dihydrate Pipecuronium Dibromide","Pipecurium Bromide","Pipecurium","Pipecuronium Bromide","Pipecuronium Dibromide, (16 alpha)-Isomer","Pipecuronium Dibromide, (17 alpha)-Isomer","Pipecuronium Dibromide, (3 beta)-Isomer","Pipecuronium Dibromide, Dihydrate","Pipecuronium, Dibromide","RGH 1106","RGH-1106","RGH1106"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D017300","description":["A piperazinyl androstane derivative which is a non-depolarizing neuromuscular blocking agent (NEUROMUSCULAR NONDEPOLARIZING AGENTS). It is used as a muscle relaxant during ANESTHESIA and surgical procedures."],"label":"Pipecuronium","obo_id":"mesh:D017300","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63077","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["1,4-Piperazinediethanesulfonic acid, monosodium salt","1,4-Piperazinediethanesulfonic acid, sodium salt (1:1)","1,4-piperazinediethanesulfonic acid sodium salt","PIPES monosodium salt","PIPES monosodium","Piperazine-1,4-diethanesulfonate, sodium salt","Sodium hydrogen piperazine-1,4-diethanesulphonate","piperazine-N,N\u0027-bis(2-ethanesulfonic acid) sodium salt","sodium 2-[4-(2-sulfoethyl)piperazin-1-yl]ethanesulfonate","sodium PIPES"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_63077","description":["An organic salt that is the monosodium salt of 2,2\u0027-piperazine-1,4-diylbisethanesulfonic acid (PIPES), a buffering agent."],"label":"monosodium PIPES","obo_id":"CHEBI:63077","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["sodium 2-[4-(2-sulfoethyl)piperazin-1-yl]ethanesulfonate"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/C031345","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["2-piperidinecarboxylic acid","L-pipecolic acid","homopipecolic acid","pipecolic acid hydrochloride, (+-)-isomer","pipecolic acid, (+,-)-isomer","pipecolic acid, (-)-","pipecolic acid, (R)-isomer","pipecolic acid, (S)-isomer","pipecolic acid, 14C-labeled cpd, (+,-)-isomer","pipecolic acid, ion (1-)","pipecolic acid, ion(1-), (+,-)-isomer","pipecolic acid, ion(1-), (S)-isomer","pipecolic acid, monopotassium salt"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_C031345","description":[],"label":"pipecolic acid","obo_id":"mesh:C031345","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_61238","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["1-(2-hydroxyethyl)piperidine","1-piperidineethanol","2-(1-piperidinyl)ethanol","2-(piperidin-1-yl)ethanol","2-Piperidinoethanol","N-(2-hydroxyethyl)piperidine","N-(hydroxyethyl)piperidine","beta-piperidinoethanol","beta-piperidylethanol"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_61238","description":["A member of the class of piperidine in which the hydrogen attached to the nitrogen atom is substituted by a 2-hydroxyethyl group."],"label":"2-(piperidin-1-yl)ethanol","obo_id":"CHEBI:61238","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["2-(piperidin-1-yl)ethanol"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C1401","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C1401","description":["A crystalline antibiotic fermentation product isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces griseoluteus with antineoplastic activity. Piperazinedione alkylates DNA at the N-7 position of guanine, inhibiting DNA replication and inducing cell cycle arrest."],"label":"Piperazinedione","obo_id":"NCIT:C1401","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["2, 5-Piperazinedione, 3,6-bis-(5-chloro-2-piperidyl)-, dihydrochloride","2, 5-piperazinedione, 3,6-bis-(5-chloro-2-piperidyl)-, dihydrochloride","2,5-Piperazinedione, 3, 6-bis(5-chloro-2-piperidinyl)-, dihydrochloride, [3S-[3.alpha.(2S*,5R*),6.alpha.(2S*,5R*)]]- (9CI)","2,5-piperazinedione, 3, 6-bis(5-chloro-2-piperidinyl)-, dihydrochloride, [3S-[3alpha(2S*,5R*),6alpha(2S*,5R*)]]- (9CI)","593A","Compound 593A","Merck Compound 593A","PZD dihydrochloride, 3,6-bis(5-chloro-2-piperidinyl)-, dihydrochloride","PZD","Piperazinedione"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C176573","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C176573","description":["A vaccine composed of autologous tolerogenic dendritic cells (DCs) loaded with the beta cell protein proinsulin peptide (PIpep), C19-A3, with potential immunosuppressive and immune-regulating activities. Upon intradermal administration, the autologous tolerogenic PIpep-loaded DCs may induce proinsulin-specific regulatory T-cells (Tregs). This may suppress the autoimmune destruction of the insulin-producing beta cells, thereby protecting the beta cells."],"label":"Autologous Tolerogenic Proinsulin Peptide-loaded Dendritic Cells PIpepTolDC","obo_id":"NCIT:C176573","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Autologous Tolerogenic DC with Proinsulin Peptide PIpepTolDC","Autologous Tolerogenic PIpep-loaded Dendritic Cells PIpepTolDC","Autologous Tolerogenic Proinsulin Peptide-loaded Dendritic Cells PIpepTolDC","PIpepTolDC Vaccine","PIpepTolDC","Proinsulin-loaded Tolerogenic DCs PIpepTolDC","Tolerogenic DC Vaccine PIpepTolDC"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_180674","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-4-(2-iodoacetamide)piperidine-N-oxyl","2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-4-[2-iodoacetamido]piperidine-1-oxyl","2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-4-iodoacetamide-piperidin-1-N-oxyl","2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-4-iodoacetamido-1-piperidinyloxy","2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidine-1-oxyl-4-(iodoacetamide)","4-(2-iodacetamido)-2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidine-1-oxyl","4-(2-iodacetamido)-2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidinyloxyl","4-(2-iodoacetamido)-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-1-piperidinooxy","4-(2-iodoacetamido)-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-1-piperidinooxyl","4-(2-iodoacetamido)-2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidine 1-oxyl","4-(2-iodoacetamido)-2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidine-1-oxyl","4-(2-iodoacetamido)-2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidinooxyl","4-(2-iodoacetamido)-TEMPO free radical","4-(N-iodoacetamide)-2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidine-1-oxyl","4-[(2-iodoacetyl)amino]-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-1-piperidinyloxy","IASL","N-(1-oxy-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-4-piperidinyl)iodoacetamide","N-(1-oxyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-4-piperidinyl)-2-iodoacetamide","N-(1-oxyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-4-piperidinyl)iodoacetamide","N-(2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-4-piperidinyl-1-oxy)iodoacetamide","N-(oxyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperid-4-yl)iodoacetamide","Synvar 101","[4-(2-iodoacetamido)-2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidin-1-yl]oxidanyl"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_180674","description":["A piperidinecarboxamide that is TEMPO carrying an 2-iodoacetamido group at position 4."],"label":"4-(2-iodacetamido)-TEMPO","obo_id":"CHEBI:180674","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["[4-(2-iodoacetamido)-2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidin-1-yl]oxidanyl"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63055","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["1,4-Piperazinediethanesulfonic acid disodium salt","1,4-Piperazinediethanesulfonic acid, disodium salt","1,4-Piperazinediethanesulfonic acid, sodium salt (1:2)","Disodium piperazine-1,4-diethanesulphonate","PIPES disodium salt","Piperazine, N,N\u0027-bis(2-ethanesulfonic acid) disodium salt","Piperazine-1,4-bis(2-ethanesulfonic acid) disodium salt","disodium 2,2\u0027-piperazine-1,4-diyldiethanesulfonate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_63055","description":["An organic salt, being the disodium salt of 2,2\u0027-piperazine-1,4-diylbisethanesulfonic acid (PIPES), a buffering agent."],"label":"disodium PIPES","obo_id":"CHEBI:63055","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["disodium 2,2\u0027-piperazine-1,4-diyldiethanesulfonate"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/C034759","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["1,3-bis(1-(7-chloro-4\u0027-quinolyl)-4\u0027-piperazinyl)propane","piperaquine phosphate (1:1)","piperaquine phosphate (1:4) anhydrous","piperaquine phosphate","piperaquine tetraphosphate anhydrous","piperaquine tetraphosphate tetrahydrate","quinoline, 4,4\u0027-(1,3-propanediyldi-4,1-piperazinediyl)bis(7-chloro-)","quinoline, 4,4\u0027-(1,3-propanediyldi-4,1-piperazinediyl)bis(7-chloro-, phosphate (1:1)","quinoline, 4,4\u0027-(1,3-propanediyldi-4,1-piperazinediyl)bis(7-chloro-, phosphate (1:4)","quinoline, 4,4\u0027-(1,3-propanediyldi-4,1-piperazinediyl)bis(7-chloro-, phosphate, hydrate (1:4:4)"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_C034759","description":[],"label":"piperaquine","obo_id":"mesh:C034759","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C124073","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C124073","description":["A nicotine analog that is an alkaloid found in tree tobacco (Nicotiana glauca) and is comprised of a pyridine substituted by a piperidin-2-yl group at position 3. Anabasine has been used as an industrial insecticide and, since it is present in trace amounts in tobacco smoke, its detection in urine can be used as an indicator of exposure to tobacco smoke."],"label":"Anabasine","obo_id":"NCIT:C124073","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["(-)-2-(3\u0027-Pyridyl)piperidine","(S)-3-(2-Piperidinyl)pyridine","-(-)-Anabasine","2-(3\u0027-Pyridyl) Piperidine","3-(2-Piperidinyl)pyridine","ANABASINE","Anabasine","L-3-(2\u0027-Piperidyl)pyridine","Neonicotine","Piperidine, 2-(3-Pyridyl)- (8CI)","Piperidine, 2-(3-Pyridyl)-","Pyridine, 3-(2-Piperidinyl)-, (S)- (9CI)","Pyridine, 3-(2-Piperidinyl)-, (S)-","Pyridine, 3-(2-Piperidyl)-","Pyridine, 3-(2-pyridyl) Piperidine","Pyridine, 3-(2S)-2-Piperidinyl-"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C1530","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C1530","description":["A combination formulation of the antibiotic piperacillin and the beta-lactamase inhibitor tazobactam with antibacterial activity. Piperacillin, a broad-spectrum, semisynthetic penicillin, binds to and inactivates penicillin-binding proteins (PBP) located on the inner membrane of the bacterial cell wall, thereby interfering with the cross-linking of peptidoglycan chains necessary for bacterial cell wall strength and rigidity. As a result, the cell wall is weakened and the cell lyses. Tazobactam, a penicillanic acid sulfone derivative, irreversibly binds to and inhibits bacterial beta-lactamase at or near its active site, thereby preventing the destruction of the beta-lactamase susceptible piperacillin by this bacterial enzyme."],"label":"Piperacillin-Tazobactam","obo_id":"NCIT:C1530","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["PIPER/TAZO","Piperacillin-Tazobactam","Piperacillin/Tazobactam","Zosyn","piperacillin-tazobactam"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_30913","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["(2S)-piperidine-2-carboxylic acid","(S)-(-)-pipecolic acid","(S)-pipecolic acid","(S)-piperidine-2-carboxylic acid","2-Piperidinecarboxylic acid","L-(-)-pipecolic acid","Pipecolic acid","Pipecolinic acid"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_30913","description":["The \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-enantiomer of pipecolic acid. It is a metabolite of lysine."],"label":"L-pipecolic acid","obo_id":"CHEBI:30913","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["(2S)-piperidine-2-carboxylic acid"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/C010176","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["(+)-halofuginone","(+-)-trans-7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-(3-hydroxy-2-piperidyl)-acetonyl)-4(3H)-quinazolinone monohydrobromide","(+-)-trans-7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-(3-hydroxy-2-piperidyl)-acetonyl)-4(3H)-quinazolinone","(-)-halofuginone hydrobromide","(-)-halofuginone","4(3H)-quinazolinone, 7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-((2R,3S)-3-hydroxy-2-piperidinyl)-2-oxopropyl)-, hydrochloride (1:1), rel-","4(3H)-quinazolinone, 7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-((2S,3R)-3-hydroxy-2-piperidinyl)-2-oxopropyl)-, hydrobromide (1:1)","4(3H)-quinazolinone, 7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-(3-hydroxy-2-piperidinyl)-2-oxopropyl)-, hydrobromide, trans-(+-)-","4(3H)-quinazolinone, 7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-(3-hydroxy-2-piperidinyl)-2-oxopropyl)-, trans-, mono(2-hydroxypropanoate)(salt)","6-chloro-7-bromo-(+)-febrifugine","6-chloro-7-bromofebrifugine","7-bromo-6-chloro-3,3-(3-hydroxy-2-piperidyl)acetonyl-4(3H)-quinazolinone-hydrolactate","7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-((2R,3S)-3-hydroxy-2-piperidinyl)-2-oxopropyl)-4(3H)-quinazolinone","7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-((2S,3R)-3-hydroxy-2-piperidinyl)-2-oxopropyl)-4(3H)-quinazolinone","7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-((2S,3R)-3-hydroxy-2-piperidyl)-2-oxo-propyl)quinazolin-4-one hydrobromide","7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-(3-hydroxy-2-piperidinyl)-2-oxopropyl)-4(3H)-quinazolinone","7-bromo-6-chlorofebrifugine","Cebegine","Halagon","Halocur","RU 19110","RU-19110","RU19110","Stenorol","chloro-bromofebrifugine","chlorobromofebrifugine","halofuginon","halofuginone HBr","halofuginone HCl","halofuginone hydrobromide","halofuginone hydrobromide, (-)-","halofuginone hydrochloride","halofuginone lactate","halofuginone monohydrobromide","halofuginone monohydrochloride","halofuginone, (+)-","halofuginone, (-)-","halofunginone","trans-7-bromo-6-chloro-3-(3-(3-hydroxy-2-piperidyl)-acetonyl)-4(3H)-quinazolinone"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_C010176","description":[],"label":"halofuginone","obo_id":"mesh:C010176","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000077725","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Piperacillin - Tazobactam","Piperacillin Tazobactam Combination Product","Piperacillin Tazobactam","Piperacillin-Tazobactam Combination Product","Pipercillin Sodium - Tazobactam Sodium","Pipercillin Sodium Tazobactam Sodium","Pipercillin Sodium, Tazobactam Sodium Drug Combination","Tazobactam, Piperacillin -","Tazocel","Tazocillin","Tazocin","Zosyn"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D000077725","description":["An antibiotic combination product of piperacillin and tazobactam, a penicillanic acid derivative with enhanced beta-lactamase inhibitory activity, that is used for the intravenous treatment of intra-abdominal, pelvic, and skin infections and for community-acquired pneumonia of moderate severity. It is also used for the treatment of PSEUDOMONAS AERUGINOSA INFECTIONS."],"label":"Piperacillin, Tazobactam Drug Combination","obo_id":"mesh:D000077725","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_139364","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["N(6)-[(2R)-2-[(2R,4S)-4-carboxy-5,5-dimethyl-1,3-thiazolidin-2-yl]-2-({(2R)-2-[(5-ethyl-2,3-dioxopiperazine-1-carbonyl)amino]-2-phenylacetyl}amino)acetyl]-L-lysine","N(6)-piperacilloyl-L-lysine","N(epsilon)-piperacilloyl-L-lysine","piperacillin-lysine"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_139364","description":["An \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-lysine derivative obtained from nucleophilic cleavage of the β-lactam ring of piperacillin by the ε-amino group of the \u003csmall\u003eL\u003c/small\u003e-lysine molecule."],"label":"piperacilloyl-